  "description": {
    "rendered": "<div style=\"width: 1080px;\" class=\"wp-video\"><video class=\"wp-video-shortcode\" id=\"video-730261-1\" width=\"1080\" height=\"1080\" preload=\"metadata\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"video/mp4\" src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/e3-pia26404-experiment-recreating-a-carbon-dioxide-plume.mp4?_=1\" /><a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/e3-pia26404-experiment-recreating-a-carbon-dioxide-plume.mp4\">https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/e3-pia26404-experiment-recreating-a-carbon-dioxide-plume.mp4</a></video></div>\n<p>This video shows Martian soil simulant erupting in a plume during a JPL lab experiment that was designed to replicate the process believed to form Martian features called \u201cspiders.\u201d When a researcher who had tried for years to re-create these conditions spotted this plume, she was ecstatic. </p>\n"
  },
  "caption": {
    "rendered": "<p>This video shows Martian soil simulant erupting in a plume during a JPL lab experiment that was designed to replicate the process believed to form Martian features called \u201cspiders.\u201d When a researcher who had tried for years to re-create these conditions spotted this plume, she was ecstatic. </p>\n"
